## Model routing (ActRouter)

The `actrouter` MCP server recommends which model fits a piece of work.

- When the user makes a new request that needs tool calls, call `route_task`
  on it first: one or two sentences on the kind of work, and your own model
  as `current_model`. If its `host_model` differs from your model, do the
  work in a sub-agent with that `model` and relay the result. Skip this for
  follow-ups such as "yes, go ahead".
- Before spawning a sub-agent for a sizeable task, call `route_task` with a
  one or two sentence description of the kind of work (no code, logs,
  secrets or file contents) and pass its `host_model` as the sub-agent's
  `model`. Use `preference: "quality"` for hard debugging, design or
  security work, and `"cost"` for bulk mechanical work.
- When writing code that calls an LLM, call `route_function` (Python) or
  `route_function_metadata` (other languages) on the function and use the
  returned `model` in the code.
- A model the user named explicitly always wins.
